                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's not bad, once you get the hang of managing your people. You need to keep in mind though that what the game considers as \"normal\" mode is, in my opinion, hard mode. And what the game considers as \"easy\" is in fact normal. \r\n\r\nThe thing to keep in mind when assigning tasks is that you shouldn't stick only to the stats each character has per skill in order to assign them somewhere. Instead, keep an eye on the relationship between these two characters. This will affect your production and survivability.\r\n\r\nOther than that, the game is simple and can become tedious once you explore around 50% of the island. When that happens, just use the need to asnwer the questions the characters of the game are also asking be your driving force. There's a lot of mystery in this game and I think it adds a lot to gameplay.",
